feat(quotes): "Save + send" combo button on draft form — copy customer link in one tap

Polish layer on the draft-quote flow per Product Director's "First Quote
in 90 Seconds" pitch. The 90-second number was a metaphor; the literal
fix is removing the round trip "save draft → list → click mark-as-sent
→ copy URL."

Now: the form has two primary actions side-by-side.
- "Save as draft" (secondary) — keeps the existing path; quote lands as
  draft; operator decides later when to share.
- "Save + send" (primary) — creates the proposal, immediately flips
  status to sent, copies the public /quote/<id> URL to clipboard, and
  toasts the URL so the operator can paste it into SMS/email/iMessage.
  When clipboard isn't available (older browsers, http context), the
  toast still shows the URL for manual copy.

Verification: typecheck + lint clean.
